  "term": "Nocturnal Paroxysmal Dystonia",
  "definition": "Nocturnal paroxysmal dystonia is a parasomnia marked by sudden episodes during non-REM sleep in which a person shows abnormal movements such as twisting, flinging, or writhing, sometimes with partly purposeful-looking activity. These episodes usually happen repeatedly over the course of a night.",
